# Multiple globs
>Now you try it. We put a few happy, but diversely-named files in /challenge/files. Go cd there and run /challenge/run, providing a single argument: a short (3 characters or less) globbed word with two * globs in it that covers every word that contains the letter p.

## Solve:
- I first read through the challenge and understood the syntax for the globs.Then implemented it to find flag. 
```
bash
hacker@globbing~multiple-globs:~$ cd /challenge/files
hacker@globbing~multiple-globs:/challenge/files$ /challenge/run *p*
You got it! Here is your flag!
pwn.college{IU6oVzvujOrulsa_Z0Q9SxiXPmk.0lM3kjNxwiM4ETOwIzW}
```

## Flag
```
put{IU6oVzvujOrulsa_Z0Q9SxiXPmk.0lM3kjNxwiM4ETOwIzW}
```

## Concepts Learnt
- Multiple glob usage is used to specify autofill for various characters.

